# coexistence.factors multiplies a whole rig's cost, so each key has to carry the worst unit's
# factor, not one unit's. k=2 and k=3 -- one and two warm documents -- were measured for the Full
# row only; lite is much the worse row at k=5 (2.293 against 1.786), so these two arms are what
# decide factors{"1"} and factors{"2"}.
#
# IR.8192 is deliberately not re-run here. Its factor at k=5 is 1.078, and a factor cannot fall as
# cores are added, so IR at k=2 or k=3 is at most 1.078 -- below the Full row's 1.136 at k=2. It
# cannot be the binding row at any k, so measuring it would cost 35 minutes to change nothing.
#
# The ranges start near the expected fit (the Full row's factors suggest ~78 and ~63) because a
# bisection that begins far below its answer spends points getting there.
bisect | lite-fit-k2 | 2 | 95 | 32 | 128 | --unit nam --model "$M/NAM Ampeg VT-40/Ampeg VT-40 - Vol 4, Bass 6, Mid 5, Treble 8, M160.nam" --slim 0.0
bisect | lite-fit-k3 | 3 | 95 | 32 |  96 | --unit nam --model "$M/NAM Ampeg VT-40/Ampeg VT-40 - Vol 4, Bass 6, Mid 5, Treble 8, M160.nam" --slim 0.0
